# Documentation & WORKLOG (always)

After **feat / fix / refactor / chore** that changes product behavior, packaging, or ops:

## Docs (same change-set)

Update the **user-facing or maintainer docs that would otherwise lie**:

| Change touches | Update at least |
|---|---|
| Installer / uninstall / path / branding | `README.md` (Download / Install / Uninstall), `PACKAGING.md`, `docs/RELEASE.md` if release steps change |
| Features / OCR / shortcuts / tray | `README.md` feature list; relevant `docs/*.md` |
| Packaging only | `PACKAGING.md` (+ README one-liner if users notice) |

Do **not** leave README claiming MSI / “OCR in progress” / wrong author when the tree has moved on. Prefer short accurate sections over emoji-heavy stale marketing.

## WORKLOG.md (granular)

Append under today’s `## YYYY-MM-DD` in repo-root `WORKLOG.md` (create the day section if missing). Prefer **several factual bullets** over one vague line:

- What changed and **why** (user-visible outcome)
- Paths / scripts / NSIS macros / flags when useful (`packaging/installer.nsh`, `scripts/make-win.js`, …)
- Follow-ups or migration notes (e.g. ghost uninstall cleanup)

Also follow skill **push-worklog** / global worklog→diary rules when a coherent chunk lands.

## Exceptions

- Pure Q&A with no durable tree change → skip docs/WORKLOG
- Typo-only in comments → skip
- Secrets never in docs or WORKLOG
